WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.698
Fritz danced and shouted but couldn't pry the baby monkey from his shoulders.

2
00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:07.673
"Stand still," I said. "You're only upsetting him."

3
00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:12.805
I pulled out a biscuit and offered a piece to the monkey, who was no bigger than a kitten.

4
00:00:12.806 --> 00:00:17.729
Finally after some coaxing, I was able to take the monkey into my own arms.

5
00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.661
"What a cute little fellow he is!" exclaimed Fritz.

6
00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:25.152
"Do let me keep him, Father. I'll call him Knips."

7
00:00:25.153 --> 00:00:32.570
The monkey settled himself on Fritz's shoulder—calmly this time—and I helped to carry Fritz's sugarcane.

8
00:00:32.571 --> 00:00:36.566
But Knips soon scrambled into Fritz's arms, which were already full.

9
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:41.132
"Come, Turk!" Fritz called, and the dog came quickly to his side.

10
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.952
"Now I need you to be a good dog."

11
00:00:43.953 --> 00:00:48.068
Fritz seated Knips on Turk's back and secured the monkey with a cord.

12
00:00:48.069 --> 00:00:52.808
Then he put a second cord around Turk's neck so he could lead the dog.

13
00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:59.163
At first neither animal was pleased with this arrangement, but they soon got used to it.

14
00:00:59.164 --> 00:01:04.104
We made our way back to camp, where my wife was preparing supper.

15
00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:08.992
"A monkey! A monkey!" cried Franz as he spied the new pet.

16
00:01:08.993 --> 00:01:12.144
"Where did you find him?" asked Ernest.

17
00:01:12.145 --> 00:01:15.160
"Why are you carrying a bundle of sticks?

18
00:01:15.161 --> 00:01:20.964
What are those strange nuts?" said Jack as he caught sight of the sugarcane and coconuts.

19
00:01:20.965 --> 00:01:24.040
Over our meal we answered all their questions.

20
00:01:24.041 --> 00:01:30.047
Although Fritz tried to feed Knips, the monkey was not interested in our meal of fish and cheese.

21
00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:37.871
But I persuaded Knips to suck liquid from a handkerchief that had been dipped in a coconut.

22
00:01:37.872 --> 00:01:41.553
The next morning I decided that Fritz and I should return to the wreck.

23
00:01:41.554 --> 00:01:47.593
Since the ship was meant to supply a colony, there were still many useful things onboard.

24
00:01:47.594 --> 00:01:53.327
I wanted to retrieve them before a storm damaged the wreck, and I wanted to check on the animals.

25
00:01:53.328 --> 00:02:03.483
Fritz insisted on taking Knips along.

26
00:02:03.484 --> 00:02:07.672
When we boarded the ship, the animals seemed glad to see us.

27
00:02:07.673 --> 00:02:12.526
We checked that they had enough food and then began examining the contents of the ship.

28
00:02:12.527 --> 00:02:18.513
We loaded some food and supplies onto our tub boat, but I kept thinking about the animals.

29
00:02:18.514 --> 00:02:22.078
"Fritz, I'm beginning to feel sorry for these poor creatures.

30
00:02:22.079 --> 00:02:26.202
I wish there were some way we could get them all ashore."

31
00:02:26.203 --> 00:02:30.479
"We could make a raft and take one or two at a time," he suggested.

32
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:37.521
"It's easy enough to say 'make a raft,' but it's quite another thing to actually make one," I pointed out.

33
00:02:37.522 --> 00:02:41.013
"Well, I can't think of anything else." Fritz frowned.

34
00:02:41.014 --> 00:02:45.388
"Unless we make them life preservers like we made for ourselves."

35
00:02:45.389 --> 00:02:47.965
"That's a good idea!" I exclaimed.

36
00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:50.044
Fritz started to laugh.

37
00:02:50.045 --> 00:02:52.394
"Really, my boy, I'm not joking.

38
00:02:52.395 --> 00:02:55.796
We could probably get all the animals ashore that way."

39
00:02:55.797 --> 00:03:00.289
So I found a fat sheep and began to put our plan into action.

40
00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.707
First I fastened a wide piece of linen around its belly.

41
00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:07.525
Next I attached some corks and empty tins to the linen.

42
00:03:07.526 --> 00:03:11.252
Then, with Fritz's help, I dropped the animal into the sea.

43
00:03:11.253 --> 00:03:16.551
It sank! But a moment later, it rose to the surface and floated perfectly.

44
00:03:16.552 --> 00:03:22.290
"Hurrah!" exclaimed Fritz. "We'll make life preservers for all the animals!"

45
00:03:22.291 --> 00:03:26.839
We then quickly caught the other animals and provided them with similar devices.

46
00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:33.820
The cow and the donkey gave us more trouble than the others because we needed something more buoyant than cork to help them float.

47
00:03:33.821 --> 00:03:39.996
But at last we found some empty casks and fastened two to each animal.

48
00:03:39.997 --> 00:03:47.258
The whole herd was now ready to start, and the donkey was the first to be launched.

49
00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:53.287
After some maneuvering, we got him into a good position, and then heaved him into the water.

50
00:03:53.288 --> 00:03:57.587
Like the sheep, he sank but immediately surfaced again.

51
00:03:57.588 --> 00:04:04.502
The cow, sheep, and goats followed him, one after another, until only the pig remained.

52
00:04:04.503 --> 00:04:07.229
But she seemed determined not to leave the ship.

53
00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:12.344
She kicked and squealed so violently that I really thought we would have to abandon her.

54
00:04:12.345 --> 00:04:16.380
Finally after much trouble, we succeeded in launching her.

55
00:04:16.381 --> 00:04:21.639
We had fastened a rope to the neck or horns of each animal.

56
00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:24.502
Ready to embark, we gathered up the ropes.

57
00:04:24.503 --> 00:04:27.977
Then we set sail, pulling our herd behind us.

58
00:04:27.978 --> 00:04:35.492
Delighted with the success of our plan, we got out some biscuits for lunch.

59
00:04:35.493 --> 00:04:39.736
While Fritz amused himself with Knips, I took out my telescope.

60
00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:44.643
I was trying to see what our loved ones were doing onshore when Fritz suddenly shouted.

61
00:04:44.644 --> 00:04:46.775
"Shark!" he cried.

62
00:04:46.776 --> 00:04:56.199
A huge shark was headed straight for one of our finest sheep.

